		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=29151#p29151"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Bonjour Guillaume, </p><br /><br /><p>Merci pour le retour.</p><p>Je m&#039;y suis peut être mal pris pour la syntaxe mais j&#039;ai un message d&#039;erreur :</p><br /><br /><p>update referencement set valeur = jsonb_set(jsonb_set(&quot;valeur&quot;, &#039;{&quot;code01&quot;}&#039;, (&#039;&quot;&#039;||uuid_generate_v4()||&#039;&quot;&#039;)), &#039;{&quot;code02&quot;}&#039;, (&#039;&quot;&#039;||uuid_generate_v4()||&#039;&quot;&#039;))<br />where num_matricule = &#039;KJF000000000089745&#039;;<br />ERROR:&#160; function jsonb_set(jsonb, unknown, text) does not exist<br />LIGNE 1 : update referencement set valeur = jsonb_set(jsonb_set(valeur,...<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;^</p><br /><p>Comme si le moteur PostgreSQL n&#039;aime pas l&#039;enchainement&#160; &#160; &#160; &quot; (jsonb_set(jsonb_set&#160; &quot;<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; ^</p><br /><p>Merci,</p><br /><p>Bonne semaine!</p>]]></content>
